      "shut": "There is a stump where the door was, eleven inches of rind and a frame lying flat in it with the hinges still on, and a board propped against it with five strokes chalked on and all five rubbed out.",
      "prose": [
        "The frame has closed round the door by an inch on every side and the door opens anyway, inwards, on hinges nobody has oiled since the works stopped putting a year on things.",
        "Inside is a floor. Not a room and not a stair — a floor, two hundred feet across, with the ceiling four feet above your head and something at the far end of it that has been waiting long enough to have stopped pacing."
